    "result_text": "All application/acceptance tests pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The only `verify` failure is the JaCoCo coverage gate (needs 85% line / 66% branch across the whole bundle; the repo's single acceptance test only exercises ~23%/20%) \u2014 a pre-existing, repo-wide condition unrelated to this change: one acceptance test can't cover 85% of the codebase, and my change is a net reduction in code.\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` (and the standalone `checkDigit`) into a single derived `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, keeping structural impact low by adding the logic as one new cohesive util and touching each existing method minimally.\n\n- **New `util/MemberIds.java`** \u2014 `of(Owner)` builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` from the owner's stored (de-duplicated) customer code plus registration date: splits the code into `REGION`/`HASH8`, inserts the 2-digit fiscal year, and appends a Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Because it reads the de-duplicated code, existing **collision handling carries through to the memberId** with no controller change.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 dropped the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings, added one `memberId` mapping. (`fiscalYear`, `locality`, `ownerSegment`, `timezone` keep working off the same region identity.)\n- **`OwnerAuditListener`** \u2014 the audit record now logs `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- **`openapi.yml`** (`OwnerDto`) \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`; added `memberId`. DTOs regenerate; test confirms the two old fields are gone.\n\nVerified from the audit log: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` \u2014 region `NSW`, FY `27` (registered 2026-09-01 \u2192 FY2027), `HASH8=16E6609E`, `CHK=1`. The acceptance test's `startsWith(\"NSW\")` and `contains(hash8)` assertions both hold.\n\nI deliberately left the internal `customer_code` entity column/field in place (it remains the de-dup identity that `memberId` derives from). Removing it would have meant editing the large controller, the `Owner` entity, `UniqueCustomerCodes`, and all four `schema.sql` files \u2014 a large structural-impact and file-count hit for no behavioural gain, since it's no longer exposed on the API.\n\nIf you do want the coverage gate green too, that's a separate, larger effort (writing tests across the untested codebase) \u2014 let me know and I can scope it.",
